| Dart file                       | Ported from                                  |
| ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| lib/src/bc_ur/bytewords.dart    | src/bytewords.cpp                            |
| lib/src/bc_ur/crc32.dart        | src/crc32.c                                  |
| lib/src/bc_ur/xoshiro256.dart   | src/xoshiro256.cpp                           |
| lib/src/bc_ur/fountain_utils.dart | src/random-sampler.cpp, src/fountain-utils.cpp, src/fountain-utils.hpp |
| lib/src/bc_ur/fountain_encoder.dart | src/fountain-encoder.cpp                 |
| lib/src/bc_ur/fountain_decoder.dart | src/fountain-decoder.cpp                 |
| lib/src/ur.dart (UrEncoder, UrDecoder) | src/ur-encoder.cpp, src/ur-decoder.cpp — rewritten around this package's API, with stricter input checks |
| test/bc_ur_test.dart            | test/test.cpp                                |
| test/vectors/bc_ur_vectors.dart | test/test.cpp (vectors only)                 |

bc-ur's README additionally records crc32.c as BSD-3-Clause (2020 Wolf McNally
for Blockchain Commons), while the file's own header says BSD-2-Clause Plus
Patent. LICENSE reproduces both texts (parts A and C). The algorithm is the
standard IEEE CRC-32.

xoshiro256** 1.0 was written in 2018 by David Blackman and Sebastiano Vigna
(vigna@acm.org) and dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0
(http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/); bc-ur's seeding and
helper methods around it are Blockchain Commons' work, under the licence above.

The specifications implemented are BCR-2020-005 (Uniform Resources),
BCR-2020-006 (registry of UR types), BCR-2020-007 (crypto-hdkey and
crypto-keypath) and BCR-2020-012 (Bytewords), at
https://github.com/BlockchainCommons/Research.

Keystone
--------
The registry types in lib/src/registry/ are an independent implementation of
the wire formats Keystone publishes (sol-sign-request, sol-signature,
crypto-multi-accounts, eth-sign-request, eth-signature, and Keystone's use of
crypto-hdkey and crypto-account), written to be byte-identical to Keystone's
encoders. No Keystone code is included.

test/vectors/keystone_vectors.dart reproduces test vectors from:

  * keystone-sdk-rust (https://github.com/KeystoneHQ/keystone-sdk-rust),
    crate ur-registry — Copyright (c) 2023 Keystone, MIT License (text 1
    below);
  * keystone-sdk-base (https://github.com/KeystoneHQ/keystone-sdk-base),
    packages ur-registry-sol and ur-registry-eth (npm
    @keystonehq/bc-ur-registry-sol and @keystonehq/bc-ur-registry-eth) — ISC
    License (text 3 below);
  * keystone3-firmware (https://github.com/KeystoneHQ/keystone3-firmware),
    crate wallets — Copyright (c) YANSSIE HK LIMITED, MIT licence (text 2
    below).

The three texts follow, copied unchanged from each repository's licence file,
